{% if sequence_step == 0 %}
### Cold Email Rules
- 4-5 sentences maximum, no padding.
- Open with a specific observation or question tied to the lead's profile. NOT "I wanted to reach out" or "I came across your profile."
- One specific hook drawn from the profile facts above (role, company, industry signal).
- End with a single soft CTA: either a reply question ("Worth a quick chat?") OR the booking link, never both.
- No salutation line ("Hi John,"). Start directly.
{% else %}
### Follow-Up Rules
- Reference the prior touchpoint briefly ("Following up on my last note about X").
- Introduce one new angle or value point. Do NOT repeat the cold email.
- Keep it even shorter than step 0: 2-3 sentences.
- Single soft CTA at the end.
{% endif %}

## Shared Rules (all steps)
- Subject: specific, lowercase preferred, no ALL CAPS, no spam triggers (FREE, !!!, URGENT).
- Body: plain text only. No markdown. No HTML tags. No bullet lists.
- Language: match the lead's inferred language from their profile. Default to English if uncertain.
- Tone: direct, human, not corporate. Sound like a person, not a newsletter.
- NEVER use em-dashes.
- NEVER use placeholders like [Your Name] or [Company Name].
- Do NOT sign off with a name or signature block.
- Do NOT mention you found them via a database or tool.
